Body, outermost first:

- `<ReaderLayout lang title={`${brand.name} — ${t.heading}`} description={t.intro} homeHref={home}>` — **no `footerNote`**: `reassurance` already renders as an answer on this page and would print twice.
- `<Masthead homeHref={home}>` + the `.seg` language switcher, `<span aria-current="true">` for the current language and `<a href="/el/faq">` / `<a href="/de/faq">` for the other; each label carries its own `lang` (WCAG 3.1.2). **Not `MemberBar`** — the FAQ is not a member section, and `MemberBar` needs a `slugs` prop this route has no place axis to supply.
- `<main class="page">`
  - `<header class="head"><h1>{t.heading}</h1><p>{t.intro}</p></header>` — `border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-divider)`, the board's double rule for a major break.
  - `t.sections.map(section => …)`:
    ```astro
    <section class="grp">
      <h2>{section.heading}</h2>
      {section.entries.map((entry) => (
        <article class="q">
          <h3>{entry.question}</h3>
          {entry.answer.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>
    ```
    The board draws `b` + `p` inside a `div`; a real heading outline is what lets a screen-reader user jump between eight questions, so `h2`/`h3` replaces it. Nothing is an accordion — every answer is open, there is no disclosure widget and no client script.
  - `<aside class="ask"><p>{t.noAnswerHere}</p><a class="btn btn-secondary btn-block" href={`/${lang}/contact`}>{t.contact}</a></aside>` — the board's `.ask` panel with the assistant sentence removed and the dead `span` turned into the link the repo can honour.

Scoped `<style>` — every value a token that exists:

```css
